//
// An ofono2mm update overwrites the patched files. Without this the phone
// keeps running the old code out of memory while the disk already holds the
// unpatched version, and only the next boot makes the difference visible -
// which is very hard to explain to yourself later.
//
// It must be DPkg::Post-Invoke. DPkg::Post-Invoke-Success parses without
// complaint, shows up in "apt-config dump", and is never run: only
// APT::Update has a -Success variant. Tested by reinstalling ofono2mm and
// finding every patch gone afterwards.
//
// Post-Invoke also runs after a failed dpkg run, hence the guards: no
// modemctl, no ofono2mm directory, nothing happens. Never fatal - apt must
// not fail because of us.
DPkg::Post-Invoke {
    "if [ -x /usr/bin/modemctl ] && [ -d /usr/lib/ofono2mm/ofono2mm ]; then /usr/bin/modemctl apply --quiet || true; fi";
};
